1
00:00:01,550 --> 00:00:04,530
Welcome to the University of Tomorrow,

2
00:00:04,530 --> 00:00:07,850
Department of Experimental Theoretical Psychology.

3
00:00:07,850 --> 00:00:13,330
This is your orientation video. It replaces the orientation seminar,

4
00:00:13,330 --> 00:00:17,370
which was cancelled when nobody could find the room.

5
00:00:17,690 --> 00:00:23,290
I'm M. Pending, Acting Deputy Assistant Registrar, provisionally.

6
00:00:23,290 --> 00:00:27,110
In the next five minutes, we'll get you set up with your professor.

7
00:00:27,110 --> 00:00:29,570
You don't need any technical background.

8
00:00:29,570 --> 00:00:32,510
The department certainly doesn't have one.

9
00:00:33,380 --> 00:00:36,180
Step one. Download the right app.

10
00:00:36,180 --> 00:00:39,300
Google makes several things called Antigravity,

11
00:00:39,300 --> 00:00:43,460
because naming things is hard, even for Google.

12
00:00:43,780 --> 00:00:46,760
Go to Antigravity.google.com.

13
00:00:46,760 --> 00:00:51,440
To the first thing on the page is called the Antigravity app.

14
00:00:51,440 --> 00:00:55,160
This is not the one. Scroll past it. Keep scrolling.

15
00:00:55,160 --> 00:00:58,620
Near the very bottom, in the smallest heading on the page,

16
00:00:58,620 --> 00:01:04,020
is Antigravity IDE, Standalone. That's the one.

17
00:01:04,020 --> 00:01:07,040
We filed a complaint about the font size.

18
00:01:07,360 --> 00:01:08,520
Choose your kind of computer.

19
00:01:08,520 --> 00:01:12,660
On Windows, the x64 button suits most everyone.

20
00:01:12,660 --> 00:01:14,680
On a Mac, choose Apple Silicon.

21
00:01:14,680 --> 00:01:18,460
If your Mac has an M-series chip, and Intel if it's older.

22
00:01:18,460 --> 00:01:23,030
The written guide shows you how to check, if you're not sure.

23
00:01:23,900 --> 00:01:27,610
On Windows, open the installer and click next until it stops asking.

24
00:01:27,610 --> 00:01:33,860
One exception. Tick “Create a desktop icon”, so you can find it again.

25
00:01:34,180 --> 00:01:39,370
On a Mac, open the file and drag Antigravity IDE into your Applications folder.

26
00:01:39,370 --> 00:01:43,630
The first time you open it, your Mac may ask whether you're sure,

27
00:01:43,630 --> 00:01:48,220
since it came from the internet. You are. Click open.

28
00:01:48,540 --> 00:01:49,290
And that's the installation.

29
00:01:49,290 --> 00:01:53,870
In point of fact, the department's own building project,

30
00:01:53,870 --> 00:01:56,950
Procrastination Hall, has been installing for 11 years.

31
00:01:56,950 --> 00:01:59,700
Opening next semester, they say.

32
00:02:00,570 --> 00:02:02,530
Antigravity will ask you to sign in with Google.

33
00:02:02,530 --> 00:02:05,190
A personal account is simplest.

34
00:02:05,190 --> 00:02:10,570
University accounts sometimes block new apps, as university accounts do.

35
00:02:10,890 --> 00:02:14,930
Then come a few setup screens. choose “Start fresh”.

36
00:02:14,930 --> 00:02:17,050
Pick any theme you like.

37
00:02:17,050 --> 00:02:22,810
And when it asks how you want to use the agent, choose Review-driven development.

38
00:02:22,810 --> 00:02:25,290
That means the AI asks before it changes anything.

39
00:02:25,290 --> 00:02:28,850
Which is more than this office does.

40
00:02:29,720 --> 00:02:33,280
A quick step out of character. Hi, I'm David Cooper.

41
00:02:33,280 --> 00:02:36,000
I'm a psychologist and I made this course.

42
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:39,730
Before we continue, a few things deserve a straight answer.

43
00:02:40,050 --> 00:02:44,260
During setup, you'll see a security notice. In plain terms,

44
00:02:44,260 --> 00:02:53,700
it says that an AI agent can read and change files and can make mistakes or be tricked into sending information somewhere it shouldn't.

45
00:02:53,700 --> 00:02:56,760
That's true of every tool like this.

46
00:02:56,760 --> 00:02:59,960
It's also why this course has one rule.

47
00:02:59,960 --> 00:03:04,360
Never put real patient or research-participant data into this

48
00:03:04,360 --> 00:03:10,400
course or into any AI tool your institution hasn't approved.

49
00:03:10,400 --> 00:03:16,170
Everything in this course is either fictional or publicly available information.

50
00:03:16,490 --> 00:03:20,270
The same screen asks whether Google can use your

51
00:03:20,270 --> 00:03:24,670
interactions to improve its That box is checked by default.

52
00:03:24,670 --> 00:03:27,780
It's your choice. Uncheck it if you prefer.

53
00:03:28,100 --> 00:03:31,760
This course is free. Antigravity's free plan has usage limits.

54
00:03:31,760 --> 00:03:37,620
So if you hit one, pause a lesson and pick up where you left off,

55
00:03:37,620 --> 00:03:44,150
or feel free to try and change to another model that you might have available to you.

56
00:03:45,020 --> 00:03:49,520
Ahem, okay, picking up where we left off.

57
00:03:50,390 --> 00:03:53,900
Next, download the course itself. The link is on the setup page.

58
00:03:53,900 --> 00:03:59,200
On Windows, you right-click the zip file, choose “Extract All”.

59
00:03:59,200 --> 00:04:03,020
Don't just open it, the files won't work from inside the zip.

60
00:04:03,020 --> 00:04:05,850
On a Mac, just double-click it.

61
00:04:06,170 --> 00:04:06,180
In Antigravity,

62
00:04:06,180 --> 00:04:13,640
choose Open Folder and pick the folder called “agentic-psychologist-main”.

63
00:04:13,960 --> 00:04:19,300
It will ask whether you trust the author of these files. Choose yes.

64
00:04:19,300 --> 00:04:22,590
Your professor needs that permission to do its job.

65
00:04:23,460 --> 00:04:28,840
And here it is. It only looks like the cockpit of a small aircraft.

66
00:04:28,840 --> 00:04:32,720
Don't panic, you really only need three parts of it.

67
00:04:33,040 --> 00:04:38,010
On the right, the agent panel. That's where you talk to your professor.

68
00:04:38,330 --> 00:04:41,010
On the left, is the Explorer.

69
00:04:41,010 --> 00:04:44,250
It's the course's filing cabinet, so to speak.

70
00:04:44,250 --> 00:04:48,610
Unlike the department’s, however, everything is where it says it is.

71
00:04:48,930 --> 00:04:53,650
In the middle is the Editor. A file opens here when you click on it.

72
00:04:53,970 --> 00:04:58,500
Everything else for right now you can safely ignore. I know we do.

73
00:04:58,820 --> 00:05:01,870
To begin, click in message box and type a forward slash,

74
00:05:01,870 --> 00:05:05,250
and then the letters s, t, a.

75
00:05:05,570 --> 00:05:08,590
You can press Tab to fill in the rest. This matters.

76
00:05:08,590 --> 00:05:11,730
On some computers, typing the whole thing doesn't work.

77
00:05:11,730 --> 00:05:14,440
But then go ahead and press Enter.

78
00:05:14,760 --> 00:05:19,810
Now, we wait. On the free plan, replies can take a minute or two.

79
00:05:19,810 --> 00:05:25,230
That's normal, and you'll see it working. No need to refresh.

80
00:05:25,230 --> 00:05:27,940
Refreshing is how we broke the coffee machine.

81
00:05:28,810 --> 00:05:30,760
When your professor wants to change a file,

82
00:05:30,760 --> 00:05:35,400
it shows you exactly what it plans to change and asks.

83
00:05:35,400 --> 00:05:38,000
Accept lets it make that one change.

84
00:05:38,000 --> 00:05:43,920
Reject means no, and nothing happens. Saying no is always safe.

85
00:05:44,240 --> 00:05:47,960
It's like reviewing a student's note before you sign it.

86
00:05:47,960 --> 00:05:51,070
Read first, then decide.

87
00:05:51,940 --> 00:05:53,350
That's orientation.

88
00:05:53,350 --> 00:05:57,570
From here, your professor takes you through it one step at a time.

89
00:05:57,570 --> 00:06:02,190
About twenty minutes a lesson. That's roughly how long the kettle takes,

90
00:06:02,190 --> 00:06:05,560
now that the coffee machine is temporarily out of order.

91
00:06:05,880 --> 00:06:08,110
If you get stuck type /im-stuck.

92
00:06:08,110 --> 00:06:12,960
To see where you are you can type /my-progress.

93
00:06:13,280 --> 00:06:17,500
Welcome to the department. We're glad you're here.

94
00:06:17,500 --> 00:06:19,120
Provisionally at least.
